  "assumptions": [
    "Microbatch size per GPU is used. Sequential gradient accumulation does not multiply saved activations; retained graphs are unsupported.",
    "No CUDA execution occurs. Loading/checkpoint/evaluation peaks, dataloader GPU prefetch, custom hooks and training-framework allocations are not individually modeled. Additional persistent storage can be supplied.",
    "Optimizer estimate excludes tiny scalar step counters; all trainable parameters are assumed optimized and receive gradients.",
    "Activation storage uses one configured compute dtype; real mixed-precision graphs can retain additional FP32 tensors.",
    "MLP saved-storage rule assumes standard eager Linear-ReLU-Linear and no custom forward hooks/operations. Shared ReLU output counted once.",
    "Regression loss assumed ordinary MSE. Auxiliary low/high include one/two extra output-sized loss buffers at >=FP32: an UNSOURCED allowance.",
    "Optimizer scratch is heuristic. Largest-parameter buffer is budgeted; foreach enabled/unknown adds ~one parameter-set buffer to high scenario. Fused/custom kernels may differ; explicit workspace overrides supported.",
    "Workspace, CUDA runtime, fragmentation and loss-buffer allowances are UNSOURCED engineering defaults, not measured or literature-prescribed percentages.",
    "Balanced byte sharding assumes one process per GPU, identical ranks and no tensor/pipeline parallelism. Buffers are replicated. Padding and ignored parameters may need explicit additional_persistent_bytes.",
    "Gathered parameters/gradients, communication and staging are conservative separate allocations; actual buffer reuse can lower memory. Transfer buffers and tiled CPU optimizer scratch are configurable planning allowances, not an emulation of framework buffer pools. Prefetch changes simultaneous residency.",
    "CPU/NVMe estimates exclude OS, dataset caches and checkpoint copies unless shared per-node bytes include them. NVMe offload requires suitable mounted storage.",
    "Full checkpoint-save, initialization and evaluation peaks are not automatically covered by steady training-state planning. Offload does not predict runtime.",
    "Legacy components/model_state_bytes describe GLOBAL unpartitioned states; state_placement and per_rank_state_bytes describe actual modeled residency."
  ],
